KG42.register("clusters-f94cc07ad3d47f6d41ae8687",{"id":"31-coalition_formation::v142-d-CL001","paper":"31-coalition_formation","label":"Dual-state participation conditions and tradable energy scope","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL001","label":"Dual-state participation conditions and tradable energy scope","market_meaning":"A prosumer may participate in state 1 without using the battery for trading; those without a battery remain in state 1. In state 1, supply and purchase correspond respectively to surplus energy and necessary energy deficit, while state 2 permits selling battery-discharge energy to peers or purchasing energy for charging. Participation eligibility, buyer purpose and product scope jointly define the transactions that can be carried out, but the state 1 quantity definition still has a source conflict.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["participation","bidding"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"The qualitative participation conditions are complementary under the same mechanism; state 1 and state 2 retain their respective conditions, and household self-use battery activity is not equated with battery participation in the market. The narrative formulas for state 1 surplus and energy deficit are inconsistent with the system model definition, and the quantitative scope has not yet been unified.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"This cluster is assembled around who may participate, what energy may be bought and sold, and their state conditions. Price decisions, coalition formation and specific payments have separate activities and results and are not merged merely because they share state labels.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Specifies energy-deficit purchasing and the demand purpose under both states, constituting the buyer part of the participation scope."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Specifies the voluntariness of participation without a battery and of battery use for trading, completing the participation eligibility and mode conditions."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Defines the product scope of state 1 surplus energy and state 2 charging/discharging energy, completing the transaction objects corresponding to participation behavior."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-CN01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003","v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g03-E27","v141-b-g03-E30"],"rationale":"The source links whether the battery is used for trading with the two types of trading states; the participation chain explains mode selection, the product chain explains the corresponding energy scope, and the two are complementary rather than constituting a dependency that the battery must be used."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-CN02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003","v141-b-g01-E008","v141-b-g01-E009"],"rationale":"The product scope and purchase purpose together cover both supply and demand sides under the two states; positive-surplus sale, necessary energy-deficit purchase and peer energy purchase for charging are retained separately, and surplus quantity and deficit quantity are not treated as the same object."}],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"This cluster uses candidate evidence permitted by the experiment; the related B entries remain unverified, and no source audit or independent C.2 review has been conducted.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003","v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g03-E27","v141-b-g03-E30"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the quoted original text and quantity definitions; candidate eligibility must not be interpreted as source or scientific content having been verified."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G02","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The state 1 surplus and energy-deficit formulas in g01-E009 are inconsistent with equations (2)-(3) of g01-E007. The equation (2) retained in R008 cannot thereby be automatically equivalent to that state 1 narrative either; R005 still provides only a qualitative purchase condition.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003","v141-c-R008::x::x_E_sur","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E008","v141-b-g01-E009"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the state 1 narrative against equations (2)-(3), and confirm how household self-use charging and discharging are counted; upstream is to handle the discrepancy, and D does not rewrite the frozen expression."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G03","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Household self-use E_{n,dis}(t) and E_{n,cha}(t) and market-traded e_{n,d}(t) and e_{n,c}(t) have different local uses and cannot be merged. The state 2 product currently consists only of components in two directions, and this chain does not clarify the optimization role of these quantities in the bidding stage or their unified units.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_E_dis","v141-c-R008::x::x_E_cha","v141-c-R008::x::x_e_c","v141-c-R008::x::x_e_d","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E006","v141-b-g01-E008","v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E012"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream is to clarify each quantity's stage role, units and self-use/trading boundary; if a scalar or net product is required, separate source support must be obtained, and it cannot be constructed independently from the component pair."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G04","category":"ontology_extension","description":"State selection currently depends on existing participation and product objects, and there is not yet an approved independent trading-state node. v141-b-g02-P01 and v141-b-g03-P01 remain proposals under review and are not approved by this assembly.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003","v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g02-E11"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g02-P01","v141-b-g03-P01"],"required_work":"Manually review the overlap and necessity of the two state proposals; if quantitative participation rules are needed, upstream is then to provide typed representations of states and purchase quantities."}]},"rule_refs":["31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R005","31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R006","31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R008"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-074ff5c1a5a28e04","COMP-acb8c66e9814835c","KG40-a6a3b767e2722b06"]});
